    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d402">

                <pb facs="0449" n="365" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg365"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. No. 814.01B</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leavell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-24T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 24, 1918, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 25, 11.41 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Guatemalan Government offers to our influential American citizen,
                        Daniel B. Hodgsdon, long-time resident of Guatemala,
                    the position of custodian of alien properties, and he has asked my advice. Would
                    the Department approve my advising him to accept? The appointment would be most
                    desirable. Please advise as soon as you can.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leavell</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
